  "schoolyard_use_notes": "Chinese Elm has small, serrated leaves that turn a vibrant yellow in the fall, making it ideal for lessons on seasonal changes and leaf identification. Its bark is mottled and exfoliates in patches, providing a tactile experience for students studying tree anatomy. The tree's resilience to various conditions can be used to discuss plant adaptation and urban forestry. Small, inconspicuous flowers appear in late summer, offering a subtle introduction to plant reproduction.",
